# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF endings.
#
# This repository's lint already refuses CRLF in the files it reads, and that catch has been
# enough for source and tests. It is not enough on its own: eslint reads no `.env` file, no
# `.cjs` seeder is exempt but no linter reads a `.gitignore` or a `.sql` either, and an editor
# writing CRLF into one of those leaves no trace until something downstream reads the file
# byte for byte.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` closes that: git normalizes on the way in whatever an editor wrote, so a
# CRLF line cannot reach a commit even where no linter is looking. Binary files are named
# explicitly so none of them is touched.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.sqlite3 binary
